y}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola in $xy$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378906 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378906 #edb/ref 1069 "q-164274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378906 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378906 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378906 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c22c6a7b-1fb3-5e18-82c2-bb58ebb939fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378906 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+{0}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =-2 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =50 \\\\ z & =\\pm 5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-5\\sqrt{2}$ and $z=5\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-5\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,0,5\\sqrt{2}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378910 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378907 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0532ee3e-209b-5f25-a2ee-3ab81c7de490" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378908 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0,0,5)$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378908 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378908 #edb/r